essential:
The brandy sequence exactly as handled:
- Julius goes first to the washstand, and Tuppence redirects him to the tantalus in the dining-room;
- Julius brings the glass and hands it to Sir James;
- Sir James forces some between her lips;
- Tuppence holds the glass while she drinks.

Talk during the vigil:
- Sir James reads the disorder as a sudden flight, perhaps on a warning from Brown;
- Julius regrets losing the photograph and vows to keep it if he ever regains it;
- Sir James supposes Jane was at the Bournemouth home under an assumed name;
- Sir James met Dr. Hall that morning, and Hall is staying at the Métropole.

